The mask construction in __init__.py is adapted from DAT's
Adaptive_Spatial_Attention.calculate_mask as distributed by Spandrel 0.4.2.
Changes include device-local allocations, dtype handling, bounded runtime
caching, cache invalidation, and ComfyUI cleanup hooks.
The optional csrc/dat_mask_cuda.cu operator directly emits the equivalent
shifted-window masks. The Python cache policy is unchanged.

The four methods in dat_layout.py are adapted from Spandrel 0.4.2's
SpatialGate.forward, Spatial_Attention.im2win,
Adaptive_Spatial_Attention.forward and Adaptive_Channel_Attention.forward.
The only computational-path changes replace eligible explicit contiguous
copies with FP32 cuBLAS transpose copies. Training/autograd and unsupported
layouts use PyTorch; Tensor methods are not patched globally.

